 },
 {
  "en": "Once you obtain 1e175 RP, 1e42 square roots, and rtu55 purchased, you can go Complex for i.<br>\n        Complex, similarly to Resetting, resets almost everything before it. You keep your Achievements<br>\n        and some things underneath the General header in the Statistics tab. i will be your most important currency from this<br>\n        point forward.<br><br>\n        <b>Base i Gain Formula:</b> (RP/1e175)<sup>0.025</sup> * (SR/1e42)<sup>0.004</sup><br>\n        After 1e200 i, base i gain past 1e200 has a square root applied. This does not affect multipliers to i gain.<br><br>\n        i has many more uses than RE, but two important uses for it is for purchasing Basic Complex Upgrades and Upgrade Points.<br>\n        The second Complex (the run after you go Complex) will feel quite slow, but Milestones and Complex Upgrades will<br>\n        speed up things quickly.",
  "kind": "exact",
  "contexts": [
   "js-other"
  ],
  "sources": [
   "textbook.js"
  ]
 },
 {
  "en": "Once you obtain 1e2950 x<sup>2</sup>, 1e660 RE, and a Root Epicenter Level √-1 completion, you can go Complex for i.<br>\n        Complex, similarly to Quadratic, resets almost everything before it. You keep your Achievements, your Challenge records,<br>\n        and some things underneath the General header in the Statistics tab. i will be your most important currency from this point forward.<br><br>\n        <b>Base i Gain Formula:</b> (((x<sup>2</sup>/1e2950)<sup>0.002</sup>)/2 + ((RE/1e660)<sup>0.004</sup>)/2)<sup>0.4</sup><br><br>\n        i has many more uses than x<sup>2</sup>, but two important uses for it is for purchasing Basic Complex Upgrades and Upgrade Points.<br>\n        The second Complex (the run after you go Complex) will feel quite slow, but Milestones and Complex Upgrades will speed up things quickly.",
  "kind": "exact",
  "contexts": [
   "js-other"
  ],
  "sources": [
   "textbook.js"
  ]
 },
 {
  "en": "Once you obtain 1e4000 circles and 1e2650 revolutions, you can go Sinusoidal for triangles.<br>\n        Sinusoidal resets everything that Integration resets. Similarly to Y-Quadratic, Sinusoidal is on the same layer as Integration,<br>\n        as they both mostly reset the same content. Triangles produce Trigonometric Waves (TW) and can purchase new upgrades.<br><br>\n        <b>Base Triangles Gain Formula:</b> 100<sup>(log<sub>10</sub>(circles)/4000) - 1</sup> * 100<sup>(log<sub>10</sub>(revolutions)/2650) - 1</sup>",
  "kind": "exact",
  "contexts": [
   "js-other"
  ],
  "sources": [
   "textbook.js"
  ]
 },
 {
  "en": "Once you obtain 1e4400 i, 1e112 y<sup>2</sup>, and 100% Mandelbrot Engine power, you can enter the Mandelbrot for<br>\n        Mandelbrot Essence (ME).<br>\n        Mandelbrot, similarly to previous layers, resets almost everything before it. You still keep some things underneath the<br>\n        General header in the Statistics tab. ME will become your most important currency from this point forward.<br><br>\n        <b>Base ME Gain Formula:</b> (i/1e4400)<sup>0.0005</sup> * (y<sup>2</sup>/1e112)<sup>0.01</sup><br>\n        After 1e100 ME, base ME gain past 1e100 has a square root applied. This does not affect multipliers to ME gain.<br>\n        ME is used for purchasing Meta-Generators and fractal spirals.",
  "kind": "exact",
  "contexts": [
   "js-other"
  ],
  "sources": [
   "textbook.js"
  ]
 },
 {
  "en": "Once you obtain 2,222y and 1 z, you can go Y-Quadratic for y<sup>2</sup>.<br>\n        Y-Quadratic resets everything that Complex resets, but also resets your sacrificed x, y, and x<sup>2</sup>. However, Y-Quadratic<br>\n        is <i>not</i> the third prestige layer! It is on the same layer as Complex, as they both mostly reset the same content.<br><br>\n        <b>Base y<sup>2</sup> Gain Formula:</b> 1.25<sup>(y-2,222)/100</sup> * 1.5<sup>z</sup><br><br>\n        y<sup>2</sup> can be spent on Y-Quadratic Upgrades, but later you will mostly use it<br>\n        for unlocking new mechanics in the Y-Quadratic tab.",
  "kind": "exact",
  "contexts": [
   "js-other"
  ],
  "sources": [
   "textbook.js"
  ]
 },
 {
  "en": "Once you obtain 70,000y and 1 z, you can go Y-Quadratic for y<sup>2</sup>.<br>\n        Y-Quadratic resets everything that Complex resets.<br><br>\n        <b>Base y<sup>2</sup> Gain Formula:</b> y/70,000 + z<br><br>\n        y<sup>2</sup> can be spent on Y-Quadratic Upgrades.",
  "kind": "exact",
  "contexts": [
   "js-other"
  ],
  "sources": [
   "textbook.js"
  ]
